<title>JAPAN: Tokyo Electric to buy 5 pct stake in uranium mine.</title>
<headline>Tokyo Electric to buy 5 pct stake in uranium mine.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tokyo Electric Power Co Inc said on Wednesday that it would buy a five percent stake in an uranium mine in Canada from the Japanese oil company Idemitsu Kosan Co Ltd.  </p>
<p>A spokesman for Tokyo Electric Power said the company would set up a subsidiary, TEPCO Resources Inc, later this month to manage its stake in the mine.</p>
<p>It is the first time that the company has purchased rights to a mine to obtain fuel for its power plants, the spokesman said.</p>
<p>The mine, which is located in the province of Saskatchewan, is expected to start producing uranium by 2000, the company said in a statement.</p>
</text>
